  "term": "methotrimeprazine",
  "definition": "Methotrimeprazine is a phenothiazine, or typical antipsychotic, with calming and sleep-promoting effects as well as anti-anxiety, anti-nausea, pain-relieving, and antipsychotic actions. It appears to work by blocking several central nervous system receptor systems, including dopamine, histamine, serotonin, cholinergic, and adrenergic receptors.",
